.PP
While running interactively, the following keys are recognised. They
are case-sensitive.
.TP
.B q
Quit immediately.
.TP
.B "<space>"
Force an immediate refresh, regardless of the configured delay.
.TP
.B P
Sort processes by descending %CPU (the default).
.TP
.B M
Sort processes by descending %MEM.
.TP
.B N
Sort processes by descending PID.
.TP
.B T
Sort processes by descending cumulative CPU time.
.TP
.B R
Reverse the current sort order.
.TP
.B c
Toggle between the short command name and the full command line in the
COMMAND column.
.TP
.B 1
Toggle between aggregate "%Cpu(s)" and per-CPU rows in the header.
.TP
.B "k, <down>"
Move the row selection down.
.TP
.B "j, <up>"
Move the row selection up.
.TP
.B "<page-up>, <page-down>"
Scroll the process table by one page.
.TP
.B "<home>, <end>"
Jump to the first or last row of the process table.
